  "body": "An operator ran `bullet demo` from `~/bullet` and got:\n\n```\nbullet: open ledger: ledger: SQLite path contains an empty or non-normal component\n```\n\nThat reads as a corrupt install. It is two separate papercuts.\n\n**The default was relative.** `data_dir()` fell back to `./target/demo`, so where the ledger resolved depended on the working directory; from a directory with no `target/` the custody check rejects the path. It now defaults to an absolute private path under `XDG_STATE_HOME` (or `~/.local/state`), and `BULLET_DATA_DIR` still wins.\n\n**`demo` created the directory group-writable.** It used `fs::create_dir_all`, which applies the umask \u2014 a default 002 yields `0775`, and the ledger then correctly refuses it with `SQLite immediate state parent must be euid-owned exact 0700`. `farm init` already creates its directory privately via `ensure_private_data_dir`; `demo` now does the same.\n\nVerified: from `~/bullet` with no environment set, `bullet demo` creates `~/.local/state/bullet/ledger` at `drwx------`, writes receipts, and exits on its honest `COMPONENT_ONLY` note. `bullet` unit tests 64/64, `cargo fmt --all --check` clean.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
